cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "OmegaFlux: daylight prediction from per-sensor geometric descriptors"
abstract: >-
  Code, simulation data and trained models for a per-sensor surrogate of annual Useful Daylight
  Illuminance. Each grid point is described by geometric descriptors of its view through the windows
  and of its position in the room (12 selected from 26 candidates), and two gradient-boosted tree
  models predict the under- and over-illuminated fractions. Includes 6,749 Radiance-simulated rooms
  (3,266,627 grid points, Warsaw climate), the experiments on transfer to unseen room shapes, a
  Radiance convergence check, a browser application and a Grasshopper service.
